{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.641,
   "text": "The man at the rental counter in Nevada slid me the keys... and one warning."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 9.241,
   "end": 15.641,
   "text": "If the GPS ever tells you to turn where there's no road... don't. And whatever you do, don't unplug it."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 16.341,
   "end": 21.547,
   "text": "I laughed. Then I drove four hundred miles of empty desert, alone, at night."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 22.247,
   "end": 26.577,
   "text": "Around two a.m., the screen flickered. In half a mile... turn left."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 27.477,
   "end": 32.427,
   "text": "There was no road. Just sand... and one porch light, far out in the dark."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 33.127,
   "end": 37.009,
   "text": "I kept driving. Turn left. Turn left. Turn left."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 37.809,
   "end": 42.097,
   "text": "Then the voice got softer. Slower. And it said my name."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 43.697,
   "end": 46.385,
   "text": "I yanked the cord out of the dash."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 47.785,
   "end": 50.921,
   "text": "The screen died. The car went silent."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 52.921,
   "end": 58.191,
   "text": "Then, way back on the empty highway behind me... a pair of headlights turned on."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 58.991,
   "end": 64.516,
   "text": "They followed me all the way home. When I pulled into my driveway at dawn, they were gone."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 65.216,
   "end": 68.032,
   "text": "I locked the door. I almost laughed."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 69.432,
   "end": 73.507,
   "text": "Then my phone lit up on the kitchen table, all by itself."
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "start": 74.807,
   "end": 76.193,
   "text": "You have arrived."
  }
 ],
